        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Co(OAc)2·4H2O (0.2 mmol, 0.0498 g), Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.05 mmol, 0.0228 g), 3-aminopropane-1,2-diol (0.1 mmol, 0.0105 g), and 2-hydroxy-1-naphthaldehyde (0.1 mmol, 0.0177 g) were dissolved in methanol (1 mL) and acetonitrile (3 mL) in a 20 cm Pyrex tube. Triethylamine (40 μL) was added, the tube was evacuated and sealed, then heated at 80 °C in an oven for 3 days. Slow cooling afforded light-brown crystals. The Schiff-base ligand H3L formed in situ.",
